# FreeBSD

These notes are historical and have not been verified on current FreeBSD
releases; the current CI workflow does not build on FreeBSD. See `INSTALL` for
general requirements and the configurations currently exercised by CI.

Use the current FreeBSD package or ports tree to install CMake 3.10+, C and C++
compilers, Bison 3.0+, Flex, GnuTLS, libgcrypt, libidn2, and SCTP development
files. SCTP can instead be disabled with `-DDISABLE_SCTP=ON`. If CMake selects
an unintended Flex executable, set `-DFLEX_EXECUTABLE=/path/to/flex`.

The historical notes mention `-DSCTP_USE_MAPPED_ADDRESSES=ON` as a workaround
for some SCTP address-handling limitations. Enable it only if required by the
SCTP stack in use; it is not a general FreeBSD requirement.
